        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Support declared MIT skill licenses",
        "body": "Closes #1377.\n\nSupports standard MIT as a stored skill license alongside MIT-0 for publish/import/API/CLI/UI surfaces. New publishes and imports detect root package.json, LICENSE, and COPYING metadata, and the summary backfill now repairs existing latest versions whose stored license defaulted to MIT-0 despite root MIT metadata.\n\nProof:\n- Publishing a skill with root package.json license MIT stores `parsed.license` as MIT.\n- Existing latest-version backfill with stored MIT-0 plus root package.json MIT patches `parsed.license` to MIT.\n- CLI inspect and SkillHeader render the stored MIT label and summary.\n- Local behavior tests passed: `VITE_CONVEX_URL=https://example.convex.cloud bun run test -- convex/lib/skillBackfill.test.ts convex/maintenance.test.ts convex/lib/skillPublish.test.ts convex/lib/githubImport.test.ts packages/schema/src/license.test.ts packages/clawhub/src/cli/commands/inspect.test.ts src/components/SkillHeader.test.tsx` reported 6 files / 100 tests passing; `bun run format:check` and `VITE_CONVEX_URL=https://example.convex.cloud bun run ci:types-build` also passed.\n- GitHub Actions on the pushed head have 23 passing non-Vercel checks; the remaining Vercel check is blocked on OpenClaw Foundation team authorization.",
